--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relationship to TypeSafe
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is an unofficial, independent client for the TypeSafe API. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by TypeSafe, and TypeSafe does not
support it.

"TypeSafe", "Jev" and "System One" are names TypeSafe uses for its company, its
models and its API, and may be trademarks of TypeSafe. They are used here only
to identify the service this software interoperates with.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Material derived from TypeSafe's API description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The wire contract this software implements -- the paths, the JSON member names,
the value types, which members are required, and the documented bounds -- is
taken from the OpenAPI document TypeSafe serves at

    https://api.typesafe.ai/openapi.json

Those are the facts any client that interoperates with the service has to use.
They reach the packages only as names and constants in compiled code.

The document itself is not included, in the packages or in the source
repository. The repository keeps the contract extracted from it
(spec/typesafe-v1/openapi.json): the document's structure with every
description, example and schema title removed, and the SHA-256 of the document
as it was served, so that a copy can be identified without being
redistributed. No description or other prose from TypeSafe's documentation is
reproduced in the packages.

The source repository's record of where TypeSafe's descriptions of the API
differ (spec/typesafe-v1/semantics.json) quotes short passages of TypeSafe's
public documentation, each attributed to its source, where they are needed to
show what each description says.
